IMPORT prelude

-- Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Part 5: the duties, permissions and prohibitions of ss 96A(1),
-- 115 (as inserted SSAA 115A(5), 115B(6)), 127(5) and 129(1), written as regulative rules (PARTY ... MUST / MAY / SHANT).
-- Layer 1, part wra4. Each has a twin decision function in another module (named in the comment above the rule) that says the
-- same thing over the facts and is the one the seat layer calls; the rules here are exercised with #TRACE.
-- Time is counted in days from the start of the period the rule measures. The text fixes who must act and the length of the
-- period, never the date, so the length is an input of each rule (the decision functions work out the length).
-- The text names no consequence for any of these duties, so none is invented: a breach is BREACH and nothing follows.
-- Where the text does not name who must make an adjustment (36B, 36D "all such payments and other adjustments shall be
-- made"), no rule is written: the passive voice names no party (fork register).

§ `s 96A -- the Secretary of State must review the sums`

DECLARE `s 96A(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 96A(1) the Secretary of State`

DECLARE `s 96A(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 96A(1) review the sums specified in section 96(5A)`

-- Twin: `s 96A(1) the five-year review is overdue` (wra4-ss96-97.l4).
-- src:1573 | (1) The Secretary of State must at least once every five years review the sums specified in section 96(5A) to determine whether it is appropriate to increase or decrease any one or more of those sums.
@ref s 96A(1) (src:1573-1573)
GIVEN `the number of days in the five years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 96A(1) party` `s 96A(1) action`
`s 96A(1) the duty to review the sums` MEANS
    PARTY `s 96A(1) the Secretary of State`
    MUST `s 96A(1) review the sums specified in section 96(5A)`
    WITHIN `the number of days in the five years`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

§ `s 115 -- withdrawing an agreement to pay a penalty`

DECLARE `s 115(2) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 115(2) the person who agreed to pay the penalty`

DECLARE `s 115(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 115(2) withdraw the agreement`

-- Twin: `s 115(2) SSAA 115A(5) the agreement is withdrawn within the cooling-off period` (wra4-ss113-116.l4). The person may
-- withdraw; leaving the permission unused is not a breach.
-- src:1915 | (2) In section 115A (penalty as alternative to prosecution), in subsection (5) (cooling-off period), for “28” there is substituted “ 14 ”.
@ref s 115(2) SSAA 115A(5) (src:1915-1915)
`s 115(2) the permission to withdraw the agreement` MEANS
    PARTY `s 115(2) the person who agreed to pay the penalty`
    MAY `s 115(2) withdraw the agreement`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

§ `s 127 -- the recipient must not supply the information onward without authority`

DECLARE `s 127(5) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(5) the recipient of the information`

DECLARE `s 127(5) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(5) supply the information to any other person or body`

-- Twin: `s 127(5) the recipient may supply the information to another person` (wra4-ss127-129.l4). With the authority the
-- prohibition does not bite (FULFILLED at once); without it the recipient SHANT supply.
-- src:2257 | (5) Information supplied under this section must not be supplied by the recipient of the information to any other person or body without—
@ref s 127(5) (src:2257-2257)
GIVEN `the recipient has the authority that is needed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 127(5) party` `s 127(5) action`
`s 127(5) the prohibition on onward supply` MEANS
    IF `the recipient has the authority that is needed`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `s 127(5) the recipient of the information`
         SHANT `s 127(5) supply the information to any other person or body`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH

§ `s 129 -- a person given information under section 128 must not disclose it`

DECLARE `s 129(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 129(1) the person to whom the information is supplied, or an employee or former employee of that person`

DECLARE `s 129(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 129(1) disclose the information`

-- Twin: `s 129(1) the bar on disclosure applies to the disclosure` (wra4-ss127-129.l4). The bar applies unless an exception
-- in (2) or (3) removes it.
-- src:2306 | (1) A person to whom information is supplied under section 128, or an employee or former employee of such a person, may not disclose the information if it relates to a particular person.
@ref s 129(1) (src:2306-2306)
GIVEN `the bar on disclosure applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 129(1) party` `s 129(1) action`
`s 129(1) the prohibition on disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the bar on disclosure applies`
    THEN PARTY `s 129(1) the person to whom the information is supplied, or an employee or former employee of that person`
         SHANT `s 129(1) disclose the information`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH
    ELSE FULFILLED
